     ll22aarrcc__mmffuuoonnllyy=00|1|2 (int)
             Controls whether only MFU metadata and data are cached from ARC
             into L2ARC.  This may be desired to avoid wasting space on L2ARC
             when reading/writing large amounts of data that are not expected
             to be accessed more than once.

             The default is 0, meaning both MRU and MFU data and metadata are
             cached.  When turning off this feature (setting it to 0), some
             MRU buffers will still be present in ARC and eventually cached on
             L2ARC.  If ll22aarrcc__nnoopprreeffeettcchh=00, some prefetched buffers will be
             cached to L2ARC, and those might later transition to MRU, in
             which case the ll22aarrcc__mmrruu__aassiizzee arcstat will not be 00.

             Setting it to 1 means to L2 cache only MFU data and metadata.

             Setting it to 2 means to L2 cache all metadata (MRU+MFU) but only
             MFU data (ie: MRU data are not cached). This can be the right
             setting to cache as much metadata as possible even when having
             high data turnover.

             Regardless of ll22aarrcc__nnoopprreeffeettcchh, some MFU buffers might be evicted
             from ARC, accessed later on as prefetches and transition to MRU
             as prefetches.  If accessed again they are counted as MRU and the
             ll22aarrcc__mmrruu__aassiizzee arcstat will not be 00.

             The ARC status of L2ARC buffers when they were first cached in
             L2ARC can be seen in the ll22aarrcc__mmrruu__aassiizzee, ll22aarrcc__mmffuu__aassiizzee, and
             ll22aarrcc__pprreeffeettcchh__aassiizzee arcstats when importing the pool or onlining
             a cache device if persistent L2ARC is enabled.

             The eevviicctt__ll22__eelliiggiibbllee__mmrruu arcstat does not take into account if
             this option is enabled as the information provided by the
             eevviicctt__ll22__eelliiggiibbllee__mm[[rrff]]uu arcstats can be used to decide if tog‐
